<title>USA: Laser Corp says FDA approves Nuvolase 660.</title>
<headline>Laser Corp says FDA approves Nuvolase 660.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY, Utah 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laser Corp said on Monday that the FDA had approved Nuvolase 660, the company's new laser-based medical system, for dermatological applications.</p>
<p>Specifically, the system can be used to treat benign cutaneous vascular and pigmented lesions, Laser Corp said in a statement.</p>
<p>The laser products company added that it has begun scheduling office demonstrations of the system to doctors and anticipates sales of its Nuvolase products in the next quarter.</p>
</text>
